# Original PNG artwork reserve

These 22 files are **not used by the current site**. They are ready for a future, separately tested image-format selection feature. The live page continues to use the WebP files one directory up.

Regenerate with `python3 tools/slice-background-png.py` from the repository root. The script crops the current `design/references/background.png` (11 main tiles and six FAQ rows) and `design/references/background_text.png` (five document thumbnails). It preserves each crop's original RGBA pixels and Adobe RGB (1998) ICC bytes, including the transparent right edge and the source overlap rows. It does not convert the color profile or edit the source images. `manifest.json` records source hashes, coordinates, dimensions, output hashes, and sizes; the script checks the decoded pixels, ICC, and matching active WebP dimensions on each run.

This folder is under `public/`, so a deployment may include its 46,308,888 PNG bytes even though the current page never requests them. Future format selection must account for network conditions, caching, correct browser color management, performance, and the same Pro/Pro Max visual and seam checks before turning these files on.
MEMORY.md:9:- CHG-0057 adds a future-use reserve of 22 exact-source Adobe RGB PNG crops in `public/art/original-png/` (46,308,888 bytes). `tools/slice-background-png.py` regenerates them and `manifest.json` records source/output hashes and crop boxes. The live page still requests WebP only; Pro/Pro Max production WebKit request logs show zero reserve PNG requests. Format switching has not been implemented.
MEMORY.md:10:- CHG-0056 replaces the temporary 22 active PNG crops with WebP derived from the **current user-modified** Adobe RGB reference through an explicit LittleCMS Adobe RGB→sRGB conversion. Every full WebP carries sRGB ICC and exact source alpha; q95 is used where measured color shift stays within thresholds, with four document thumbnails lossless. The old `public/art/unused-webp/` archive and superseded active PNG crops were removed; `design/references/background.png` and the user's untracked `background_old.png` were preserved. `tools/convert-art-webp.py` regenerates the files and [color metrics](docs/evidence/art-webp/color-metrics.json); the method and alternatives are in [art color pipeline](docs/art-color-pipeline.md).
